### =====================================================================
### END-TO-END (Phase 9): delivery partners, through the API gateway (port 8080)
###
###   A. A new partner registers -> KYC -> admin rejects, partner fixes it -> admin approves -> online
###   B. ONLINE order: delivery1 rejects it -> reassigned to the new partner -> customer not at home
###      -> DELIVERY_FAILED: stock released, money refunded, both sides notified -> items returned to the store
###   C. Nobody online -> the delivery waits -> admin assigns it -> COD delivered with a proof photo -> earnings
###   D. The customer cancels while the partner is on the way to the store -> the delivery is cancelled
###
### Needs: infrastructure + every service of Phases 1-9 + the connectors (scripts\register-connectors.ps1).
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run the requests IN ORDER.
### Every run registers a new delivery partner ({{$timestamp}} makes the email unique).
### =====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@customer2Token = {{customer2Login.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@vendorToken = {{vendorLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@partnerToken = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@newPartnerToken = {{newPartner.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@newPartnerId = {{newPartner.response.body.$.data.user.id}}
@failedOrderId = {{failedOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}
@failedDeliveryId = {{offeredToDelivery1.response.body.$.data.content[0].id}}
@codOrderId = {{codOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}
@codDeliveryId = {{waiting.response.body.$.data.content[0].id}}
@proofUrl = {{proof.response.body.$.data.proofPhotoUrl}}
@cancelOrderId = {{cancelOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. customer1 (user 4) logs in
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 2. customer2 (user 7) logs in
# @name customer2Login
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer2@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 3. vendor1 (Fresh Mart, store 1, PIN 560038 = zone 1 Indiranagar) logs in
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 4. The admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 5. delivery1 (Arjun Singh, user 5, zone 1) logs in
# @name partnerLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "delivery1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### ===== A. A new delivery partner joins =====

### 6. Neha registers as a delivery partner (public) -> UserRegistered
# @name newPartner
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Neha Gupta",
  "email": "neha.{{$timestamp}}@example.com",
  "phone": "8{{$randomInt 100000000 999999999}}",
  "password": "Password@123",
  "role": "DELIVERY_PARTNER"
}


### 7. (wait) delivery-service created her profile from UserRegistered: KYC NOT_SUBMITTED
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 8. Going online before the KYC is approved -> 400
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 9. KYC with mistakes -> 400 with one error per field
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile/kyc
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicleType": "SCOOTER",
  "vehicleNumber": "my scooter",
  "drivingLicenseNumber": "",
  "zoneId": null
}


### 10. KYC for zone 1 (Indiranagar) -> PENDING
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile/kyc
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicleType": "SCOOTER",
  "vehicleNumber": "KA03MN4521",
  "drivingLicenseNumber": "KA0320210004521",
  "zoneId": 1
}


### 11. Admin: partners waiting for a KYC decision
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners?kycStatus=PENDING
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 12. Admin rejects it with a reason -> REJECTED
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{newPartnerId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "The driving licence number does not match the photo"
}


### 13. Neha sends corrected details -> PENDING again
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile/kyc
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicleType": "SCOOTER",
  "vehicleNumber": "KA03MN4521",
  "drivingLicenseNumber": "KA0320210004512",
  "zoneId": 1
}


### 14. Admin approves -> APPROVED
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/delivery-partners/{{newPartnerId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 15. Neha goes online (for 30 minutes)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### ===== B. Rejected, reassigned, delivery failed -> compensation =====

### 16. delivery1 goes online too (zone 1 now has two online partners; the lowest user id is asked first)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 17. customer1 starts with an empty cart
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 18. ...adds 2 dozen bananas (2 x 60.00)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 4,
  "quantity": 2
}


### 19. ...and orders ONLINE to the HOME address (1)
# @name failedOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "ONLINE"
}


### 20. (wait) Stock reserved -> AWAITING_PAYMENT; pay with the mock gateway -> PAID
# @wait 4
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{failedOrderId}}/mock-pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "success": true
}


### 21. (wait) vendor1 accepts the CONFIRMED order
# @wait 3
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{failedOrderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 22. ...packs it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{failedOrderId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 23. ...and hands it over -> OrderReadyForPickup
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{failedOrderId}}/ready-for-pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 24. (wait) delivery-service created the delivery and offered it to delivery1 (ASSIGNED)
# @wait 3
# @name offeredToDelivery1
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 25. delivery1 rejects it -> it goes straight to Neha
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 26. Neha's current delivery: the same one, ASSIGNED to her
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 27. (wait) Neha got a "New delivery" notification (in-app + email)
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 28. delivery1 can no longer act on it -> 404 (a partner only sees their own deliveries)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 29. Neha accepts it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 30. ...picks it up (order OUT_FOR_DELIVERY)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/pick-up
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 31. ...drives to the customer
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 32. Nobody at the door -> FAILED (DeliveryFailed)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/issue
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "issue": "CUSTOMER_UNAVAILABLE",
  "note": "Nobody at the door, phone switched off"
}


### 33. (wait) The order is DELIVERY_FAILED; the online payment was refunded -> paymentStatus REFUNDED
# @wait 6
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{failedOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 34. payment-service: REFUNDED (refundReference mock_refund_...)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{failedOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 35. inventory-service: the bananas are not reserved any more
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/4
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 36. Neha brings the items back to the store -> RETURNED (she is free for the next delivery)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{failedDeliveryId}}/return
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 37. customer1 was told: delivery failed, refund
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 38. vendor1 was told: not delivered, items come back
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### ===== C. Nobody online -> admin assigns; cash on delivery with a proof photo =====

### 39. delivery1 goes offline
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/offline
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 40. Neha goes offline
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/offline
Authorization: Bearer {{newPartnerToken}}


### 41. customer2 (user 7) starts with an empty cart
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}


### 42. ...adds 3 x Lay's (3 x 20.00)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 9,
  "quantity": 3
}


### 43. ...and 1 x Surf Excel (195.50)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 10,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 44. ...orders COD to the HOME address (3, PIN 560008)
# @name codOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 3,
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}


### 45. (wait) vendor1 accepts the CONFIRMED order
# @wait 4
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{codOrderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 46. ...packs it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{codOrderId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 47. ...and hands it over
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{codOrderId}}/ready-for-pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 48. (wait) Admin: nobody is online, so the delivery waits (WAITING_FOR_PARTNER)
# @wait 3
# @name waiting
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries?status=WAITING_FOR_PARTNER
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 49. Admin assigns it to delivery1 by hand -> ASSIGNED (DeliveryAssigned)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries/{{codDeliveryId}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "partnerUserId": 5
}


### 50. delivery1 accepts it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{codDeliveryId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 51. ...picks it up
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{codDeliveryId}}/pick-up
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 52. ...drives to the customer
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{codDeliveryId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 53. ...takes a photo of the handed-over bag (proof of delivery)
# @name proof
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{codDeliveryId}}/proof
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=GroceryBoundary

--GroceryBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="proof.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./assets/sample-product.png
--GroceryBoundary--


### 54. ...collects 255.50 in cash and delivers -> DELIVERED, payout 40.00
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{codDeliveryId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 55. (wait) customer2's order: DELIVERED by Arjun Singh, paymentStatus PAID (cash collected)
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{codOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}


### 56. payment-service: COLLECTED
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{codOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}


### 57. The proof photo, through the gateway (any logged-in user)
GET {{proofUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}


### 58. delivery1's earnings this month (one line per day, India time)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/earnings?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 59. delivery1's completed deliveries
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=false
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### ===== D. Cancelled while the partner is on the way to the store =====

### 60. delivery1 goes online
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 61. customer1 adds 3 kg of tomatoes (3 x 36.00)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 3
}


### 62. ...orders COD
# @name cancelOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}


### 63. (wait) vendor1 accepts it
# @wait 4
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 64. ...packs it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 65. ...and hands it over
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/ready-for-pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 66. (wait) The order shows delivery1 as its partner (DeliveryAssigned)
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 67. The customer cancels: still allowed, nothing was picked up -> CANCELLED
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Ordered the wrong quantity"
}


### 68. (wait) delivery1 has no current delivery any more (the delivery is CANCELLED)
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 69. Admin: every delivery of Neha (one RETURNED)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/deliveries?partnerUserId={{newPartnerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 70. CLEAN UP: delivery1 goes offline
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/offline
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
